      "id": "s3",
      "title": "Cool cities: The value of urban trees",
      "publisher": "Elsevier BV",
      "author": "Han, Lu; Heblich, Stephan; Timmins, Christopher",
      "published_at": "2024",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.4702277",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T15:48:53.368Z",
      "sha256": "e1f9ef0687f51130e68e614f2429d75e08b90643538a13ff2d5b39979e9be74f",
      "rendered": false,
      "scraped": false,
      "excerpts": [
        "This paper estimates the value of urban trees and shows their ability to moderate temperatures during heatwaves and reduce energy consumption.",
        "Trees significantly cool urban areas and save energy, but their total amenity value surpasses the value of these ecosystem services, highlighting their cost-effectiveness in combating urban heat island effects."
      ]
